// The values a Float can hold that a naive formatter mishandles, and the
// clamps at both ends of `places`. `0.0 / 0.0` is NaN and `1.0 / 0.0` is
// infinity; a formatter that errored on them would be worse than one that
// shows them.
fn main() {
    println((0.0 / 0.0).fixed(2))
    println((1.0 / 0.0).fixed(2))
    println((-1.0 / 0.0).fixed(2))
    println((1.75).fixed(-1))
}
